# Build output
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Ll]og/
[Ll]ogs/

# Visual Studio
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs
*.rsuser
*.DotSettings.user

# Debug launch profiles. Visual Studio writes Properties/launchSettings.json when the project is launched
# from the IDE; here it recorded "commandLineArgs": "--sim", which is a per-machine debugging convenience
# and not project state that a build or a test depends on. The leading **/ is load-bearing: a pattern with
# a separator in its middle is anchored to this file's own directory, so "Properties/launchSettings.json"
# alone would match only <repo-root>/Properties/ and silently miss EchoEnvironment/Properties/. If a launch
# profile ever needs to be shared across machines deliberately, un-ignore this path rather than deleting
# the rule.
**/Properties/launchSettings.json

# Tests
TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage

# Packages
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
packages/

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.log
*.bak
*.swp

# Capture drops. The capture tee writes into the executable's own captures folder, which [Bb]in/
# already swallows; this rule is for copies parked at the repo root, which nothing else ignores.
# It does NOT cover the checked-in fixture, which lives in EchoEnvironment.Tests/TestData and is
# deliberately tracked.
captures/

# MCP server state. Not part of the project and not something a build or a test depends on. Until
# this rule existed every status report in MIGRATION_PLAN.md had to say "clean apart from untracked
# .mcp/", which is the same problem the empty EchoEnvironment/Math directory caused: a tree that is
# not actually dirty being described, every time, as if it might be.
.mcp/
